# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the TechIT Inventory Next.js application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0`
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Installation Method**: Followed official Vercel documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart

### 2. Files Modified

#### `app/layout.js`
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/next'`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag
- Followed Next.js App Router integration pattern as specified in the official documentation

#### `package.json`
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version ^2.0.0 to dependencies

#### `package-lock.json`
- Updated with the new package and its 413 dependencies
- Lock file ensures consistent dependency resolution across environments

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.2.9 (App Router)
- **Integration Type**: Next.js-specific component (`@vercel/speed-insights/next`)
- **Placement**: Added SpeedInsights component to root layout as recommended for Next.js v13.5+

### Documentation Source
Retrieved the latest installation instructions from the official Vercel documentation to ensure the most up-to-date setup process was followed.

### Verification Steps Completed
✅ Build completed successfully (no compilation errors)
✅ Linter ran with no new errors in modified file (app/layout.js)
✅ Dependencies installed correctly
✅ Lock file updated properly

## Next Steps for User

To complete the Speed Insights setup:

1. **Enable Speed Insights in Vercel Dashboard**
   - Navigate to your project in the Vercel dashboard
   - Go to Speed Insights section
   - Click "Enable" to activate the feature
   - This will create the necessary routes at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`

2. **Deploy the Application**
   - Push these changes to your repository
   - Vercel will automatically deploy the updates
   - Or manually deploy using: `vercel deploy`

3. **View Metrics**
   - After deployment and user traffic, metrics will be available in the Vercel dashboard
   - Access them under the Speed Insights section for your project

## Technical Notes

- The SpeedInsights component is placed at the end of the body tag for optimal performance
- It will automatically track Core Web Vitals and other performance metrics
- The tracking script appears as `/<unique-path>/script.js` in the page head after deployment
- Speed Insights is available on all Vercel plans (including free tier)
- No additional configuration is required - the component works out of the box

## Compatibility

- ✅ Next.js 16.2.9 (App Router)
- ✅ React 19.2.3
- ✅ Latest @vercel/speed-insights v2.0.0
